From: SriAkhilSJ <206201543+SriAkhilSJ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 11:50:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs(preview): unstack the two doc comments my last commit
 left on one declaration
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Re-reading d1c64cca found a defect it introduced: the insert put `workspacePath` between
`resolveEndpoint`'s doc comment and `resolveEndpoint` itself. TypeScript attaches a JSDoc block to the
declaration that follows it, so the result was two stacked comments over the getter and a
`resolveEndpoint` with no documentation at all — the comment that explains why it filters endpoints by
workspace ("a preview server started for THIS folder is the one worth framing") was sitting on the
getter, where it is wrong.

Comments moved back to the declarations they describe. Checked mechanically rather than by eye: no
JSDoc block in the file is followed by another block or by a blank line, and both `workspacePath` and
`resolveEndpoint` have exactly one comment directly above them. Gate A: Crusor errors: 0.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../contrib/crusorai/browser/crusorAIPreviewService.ts | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/desktop/vscode/src/vs/workbench/contrib/crusorai/browser/crusorAIPreviewService.ts b/desktop/vscode/src/vs/workbench/contrib/crusorai/browser/crusorAIPreviewService.ts
index 3e393768..97b4ae80 100644
--- a/desktop/vscode/src/vs/workbench/contrib/crusorai/browser/crusorAIPreviewService.ts
+++ b/desktop/vscode/src/vs/workbench/contrib/crusorai/browser/crusorAIPreviewService.ts
@@ -152,11 +152,6 @@ export class CrusorAIPreviewService extends Disposable implements ICrusorAIPrevi
 		return URI.joinPath(this.pathService.userHome({ preferLocal: true }), '.crusorai', ...ENDPOINT_DIR);
 	}
 
-	/**
-	 * The freshest published endpoint for this workspace. The proxy writes one file per session, and
-	 * the workbench is not told which session id owns the local proxy, so the workspace path decides:
-	 * a preview server started for THIS folder is the one worth framing.
-	 */
 	/**
 	 * The folder this session is bound to, by the contribution's P0 rule (the same one
 	 * `crusorAIRendererService.sessionFolder` applies to the composer): zero folders means no
@@ -172,6 +167,11 @@ export class CrusorAIPreviewService extends Disposable implements ICrusorAIPrevi
 		return folders.length === 1 ? folders[0].uri.fsPath : undefined;
 	}
 
+	/**
+	 * The freshest published endpoint for this workspace. The proxy writes one file per session, and
+	 * the workbench is not told which session id owns the local proxy, so the workspace path decides:
+	 * a preview server started for THIS folder is the one worth framing.
+	 */
 	private async resolveEndpoint(): Promise<CrusorPreviewEndpoint | undefined> {
 		const open = this.workspaceService.getWorkspace().folders.map(folder => folder.uri.fsPath);
 		if (!open.length) {
